---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EditorialByline from '../../components/EditorialByline.astro';
import { dataLastmod, stats, fmtDate } from '../../lib/data.js';
---
<Base title="Government processing-time reports — GovWait" description="Source-backed baseline and change reports for Canadian, UK and New Zealand visa and government processing times.">
  <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › Reports</nav>
  <h1>Processing-time reports</h1>
  <p class="lede">Original analysis from GovWait’s append-only dataset: what each government publishes now, where the widest gaps sit, and what changes after a second observation exists.</p>
  <EditorialByline published="2026-08-23" checked={dataLastmod} label="Latest represented data" />

  <div class="callout good"><span class="report-status">Baseline release</span><p>The dataset currently contains its first observation. These reports therefore establish an honest baseline rather than inventing movement. Each will begin listing increases and decreases automatically when an official value differs on a later verified refresh.</p></div>

  <ul class="grid">
    <li><a class="t" href="/reports/canada-processing-time-changes/">Canada processing-time baseline &amp; changes</a><p class="small muted">Country coverage, medians, ranges and future IRCC movements by service.</p></li>
    <li><a class="t" href="/reports/uk-visa-processing-time-changes/">UK visa-standard baseline &amp; changes</a><p class="small muted">Inside-versus-outside comparisons and the current UKVI standard distribution.</p></li>
    <li><a class="t" href="/reports/new-zealand-visa-processing-time-changes/">New Zealand visa baseline &amp; changes</a><p class="small muted">The gap between INZ’s 50% and 80% completion points across reviewed visas.</p></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to cite a report</h2>
  <p>Link the permanent report URL, name the government agency, and include the data date shown on the report. The report should not be described as a promise about an individual application.</p>
  <p class="small muted">Dataset generated {fmtDate(stats.generated_at)} · {stats.entities.toLocaleString()} routes · {stats.observations.toLocaleString()} observations.</p>
</Base>
